#AUTO 102
#NEEDED 1
# Dynamic SD bus-speed select + validation — issue 110l.
#
# Rather than hardcode a speed, sd_select_speed (in src/015-sdmmc.c) reads
# what the card supports (4-bit? High-Speed?), weighs it against the host's
# ceiling at the current 3.3V signalling (High-Speed; UHS needs a 1.8V
# switch we haven't built), logs all three inputs, and applies the safe
# minimum — for this card, 4-bit + High-Speed (50 MHz). Then it re-runs the
# proven IDMAC write-read round-trip AT the new speed to confirm transfers
# still land cleanly when the bus is faster and wider.
#
# Read the log for the decision lines ("card width", "card speed", "host
# ceiling", and the "-> applied" results) and then the round-trip verdict:
#   IDMAC WRITE OK (read-back matches the non-zero pattern)  = transfers
#     work at 4-bit / 50 MHz, so the dump's write side is now ~8x faster
#   MISMATCH / INCONCLUSIVE / a switch FAILED = the faster bus or the
#     mode switch needs a look (the per-step logs + RINTSTS point the way)
#
# Safe — the round-trip writes only the reserved LBA 0x300000. Needs the
# sd_speed + sd_dma CALL targets (probe engine 019).

CALL sd_init
CALL sd_speed
CALL sd_dma
